  "solution": "Given:\n\nx + 2y = 14\nx − y = 5\n\nCalculations:\n\nFrom the second equation:\nx = 5 + y\n\nSubstitute into the first equation:\n5 + y + 2y = 14\n\n5 + 3y = 14\n\n3y = 9\n\ny = 3\n\nNow substitute back:\nx = 5 + 3\nx = 8\n\n∴ The correct answer is 'Option 3.'",
